60,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The options are on the table. I lean toward per-room metering, but the cost is steep.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, I’m worried about the workload. If we pick metering, who actually logs the readings every month?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, I find the per-room metering appealing for fairness, but I worry the shared area costs will still cause friction.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"@Benjamin, I cannot support the upfront cost of metering. I need a structure that stabilizes my winter expenses without a large initial investment.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, I hear you. I just want a way that stops the arguments without making anyone feel watched or blamed.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mio, the other house spent forty minutes on it. It’s manageable if we rotate the duty, so no one carries it alone.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, forty minutes sounds okay, but I’m still scared of the monthly demands. I’d rather not be the one chasing people for money.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, the shared area is small. If we split that fairly, the friction disappears. The private meters handle the rest.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Benjamin, forty minutes is fine, but the 34,000 yen per room is not. I cannot justify that expense when the usage gap is largely behavioral.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Mio, I agree. Maybe we can pick a system where nobody has to chase anyone, so the air stays calm.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, I understand the cost concern. But the seasonal option still leaves winter bills unpredictable, which is exactly what I want to avoid.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mio,,"- **Mio**: @Benjamin, but if we fix the rate, I don’t have to chase anyone for extra money. That sounds much safer for me.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: @Mio, a fixed rate does remove the monthly chasing. I can live with that, provided the year-end settlement is simple.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, exactly. A fixed seasonal rate protects me from the winter spike without the upfront metering cost. I can support that.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minato,,"- **Minato**: @Mio, I like that too. If the amount is fixed, nobody has to send scary reminders. It feels much safer for us.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"- **Benjamin**: @Mio, I concede. The fixed rate removes the monthly friction and the upfront cost. I will vote for the seasonal option.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Mio,,"- **Mio**: @Benjamin, thank you. I am voting for the seasonal fixed rate. It feels the most peaceful for all of us.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: @Benjamin, I agree. The seasonal fixed rate seems the most balanced. I am voting for it as well.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Benjamin, I am voting for the seasonal fixed rate. It stabilizes my winter costs without the expensive upfront investment I cannot justify.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minato,,"@Benjamin, I am voting for the seasonal fixed rate too. It feels calm and fair, and I hope it helps us stay friends.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
